## What this repo carries

{% if workflow_profile == 'spec-driven' -%}
- **Planning process** — OpenSpec (`openspec/`) provides proposals, plans, tasks,
  validation, and archival for non-trivial changes.
{% else -%}
- **Planning process** — acceptance criteria live in pull requests; non-trivial or
  high-risk work uses a proportional plan in `docs/changes/`.
{% endif -%}
- **Agent rulebook** — one source in `.ruler/`, fanned out to {{ agents | join(', ') }}.
- **Definition-of-done gate** — work is not "done" until the plan is satisfied and tests
  exist in the right place, of the right type, and pass.
- **Repository contract** — `.agent-standard/manifest.json` declares commands, docs, skills,
  ownership, repository platform, conformance state, security profile, waivers, and the required CycloneDX/SPDX bill of materials.
{% if mode == 'greenfield' %}- **Project skeleton** — a {{ architecture }} layout for {{ language_stack }}.{% endif %}

## Working here

{% if language_stack == 'ts-node' or language_stack == 'ts-next' -%}
```bash
npm install
npm run sbom
npm run agent:verify
```
{% elif language_stack == 'py-fastapi' -%}
```bash
uv sync
node .agent-standard/scripts/sbom.mjs --write
node .agent-standard/scripts/verify.mjs
```
{% endif -%}

The gate runs fast tests locally (a Claude Code stop hook) and the complete contract{{ " " }}
{%- if ci %}as a CI job intended to be required by {% if repository_platform == 'github' %}a GitHub ruleset{% else %}an Azure Repos Build Validation policy{% endif %}{% else %}— CI enforcement is disabled for this repo{% endif %}.
The manifest keeps local results separate from remotely audited enforcement, so a green local run does not overclaim conformance.

## Updating the standard

```bash
copier update --trust --answers-file .agent-standard/copier-answers.yml
```

After an update, reinstall dependencies, refresh the SBOM, run the manifest verification
command, and commit the generated agent files. They are intentionally tracked so a fresh
clone receives the same instructions and skills.
